# armour/man/brigandine_hang: the brigandine's skirt on the man (ARMOUR-M, wave 2 r1): plate_hang's two stepped panels as
# the coat's riveted cloth skirt (accent, a rivet course on the second row), hinged at the belt with the fork between them.
# Base views keep plate_hang's mask in every hang key (rest wide flare lie idle sit floor kneel ride breeze); every `when`
# view of T5 / T6 / Mythic and the layers is plate_hang's own, copied; its forge (hero) tassets and edge overlays are not
# (steel over the cloth, and only in rest / idle / breeze): the forge edge tiles dress the hem. Keys: the hang channel in D U R L.
# Generated by ARMOUR-M tools/gen_brig.py from plate_hang.pxm; re-run, never hand-edit. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body man
role armour brigandine
layer hangFront
anchor hip
keys hang
z 10
legend Q linen 0
legend R linen 1
legend S linen 2
legend T linen 3
legend U linen 4
legend J cloak 0
legend D cloak 1
legend H cloak 2
legend I cloak 3
legend X cloak 4
legend k device 1
legend l device 2
legend F device 3

